#: src/vim.md:3
msgid "Vim Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed includes a Vim emulation layer. This page covers enabling and disabling "
"vim mode, key bindings, Zed-specific features, and configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:7
msgid "Zed's vim mode design"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:9
msgid ""
"Vim mode replicates the behavior of motions and commands where it makes "
"sense and uses Zed-specific functionality where Zed's approach is better. "
"The goal is a familiar experience that works out of the box without "
"requiring configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:11
msgid ""
"This includes support for semantic navigation, multiple cursors, or other "
"features usually provided by plugins like surrounding text."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:13
msgid ""
"So, Zed's vim mode does not replicate Vim one-to-one, but it meshes Vim's "
"modal design with Zed's modern features to provide a more fluid experience. "
"It's also configurable, so you can add your own key bindings or override the "
"defaults."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:15
msgid "Core differences"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:17
msgid ""
"There are four types of features in vim mode that use Zed's core "
"functionality, leading to some differences in behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:19
msgid ""
"**Motions**: vim mode uses Zed's semantic parsing to tune the behavior of "
"motions per language. For example, in Rust, jumping to matching bracket with "
"`%` works with the pipe character `|`. In JavaScript, `w` considers `$` to "
"be a word character."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:20
msgid ""
"**Visual block selections**: vim mode uses Zed's multiple cursor to emulate "
"visual block selections, making block selections a lot more flexible. For "
"example, anything you insert after a block selection updates on every line "
"in real-time, and you can add or remove cursors anytime."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:21
msgid ""
"**Macros**: vim mode uses Zed's recording system for vim macros. So, you can "
"capture and replay more complex actions, like autocompletion."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:22
msgid ""
"**Search and replace**: vim mode uses Zed's search system, so, the syntax "
"for regular expressions is slightly different compared to Vim. [Head to the "
"Regex differences section](#regex-differences) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:24
msgid ""
"**Note:** The foundations of Zed's vim mode should already cover many use "
"cases, and we're always looking to improve it. If you find missing features "
"that you rely on in your workflow, please [file an issue on GitHub](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues)."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:26
msgid "Enabling and disabling vim mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:28
msgid ""
"When you first open Zed, you'll see a checkbox on the welcome screen that "
"allows you to enable vim mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:30
msgid ""
"If you missed this, you can toggle vim mode on or off anytime by opening the "
"command palette and using the workspace command `toggle vim mode`."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:32
msgid ""
"**Note**: This command toggles the following property in your user settings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:36
msgid "\"vim_mode\""
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:40
msgid "Zed-specific features"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:42
msgid ""
"Zed is built on a modern foundation that (among other things) uses Tree-"
"sitter and language servers to understand the content of the file you're "
"editing and supports multiple cursors out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:44
msgid ""
"Vim mode has several \"core Zed\" key bindings that will help you make the "
"most of Zed's specific feature set."
msgstr ""

