#: src/vim.md:182
msgid "AnyQuotes and AnyBrackets (Traditional Vim behavior)"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:184
msgid "These text objects implement traditional Vim behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:186
msgid ""
"**Selection priority**: Finds the innermost (closest) quotes or brackets "
"first"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:187
msgid ""
"**Fallback mechanism**: If none are found, falls back to the current line"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:188
msgid ""
"**Character-based matching**: Focuses solely on open and close characters "
"without considering syntax"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:189
msgid ""
"**Vanilla Vim similarity**: AnyBrackets matches the behavior of commands "
"like `ci<`, `ci(`, etc., in vanilla Vim, including potential edge cases "
"(like considering `>` in `=>` as a closing delimiter)"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:191
msgid "MiniQuotes and MiniBrackets (mini.ai behavior)"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:193
msgid ""
"These text objects implement the behavior of the [mini.ai](https://github."
"com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-ai.md) Neovim plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:195
msgid ""
"**Selection priority**: Searches the current line first before expanding "
"outward"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:196
msgid ""
"**Tree-sitter integration**: Uses Tree-sitter queries for more context-aware "
"selections"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:197
msgid ""
"**Syntax-aware matching**: Can distinguish between actual brackets and "
"similar characters in other contexts (like `>` in `=>`)"
msgstr ""

