#: src/vim.md:662
msgid "Regex differences"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:664
msgid ""
"Zed uses a different regular expression engine from Vim. This means that you "
"will have to use a different syntax in some cases. Here are the most common "
"differences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:666
msgid ""
"**Capture groups**: Vim uses `\\(` and `\\)` to represent capture groups, in "
"Zed these are `(` and `)`. On the flip side, in Vim, `(` and `)` represent "
"literal parentheses, but in Zed these must be escaped to `\\(` and `\\)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:667
msgid ""
"**Matches**: When replacing, Vim uses the backslash character followed by a "
"number to represent a matched capture group. For example, `\\1`. Zed uses "
"the dollar sign instead. So, when in Vim you use `\\0` to represent the "
"entire match, in Zed the syntax is `$0` instead. Same for numbered capture "
"groups: `\\1` in Vim is `$1` in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:668
msgid ""
"**Global option**: By default, in Vim, regex searches only match the first "
"occurrence on a line, and you append `/g` at the end of your query to find "
"all matches. In Zed, regex searches are global by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:669
msgid ""
"**Case sensitivity**: Vim uses `/i` to indicate a case-insensitive search. "
"In Zed you can either write `(?i)` at the start of the pattern or toggle "
"case-sensitivity with the shortcut <kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-cmd-c\\|alt-"
"c</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:671
msgid ""
"**Note**: To help with the transition, the command palette will fix "
"parentheses and replace groups for you when you write a Vim-style substitute "
"command, `:%s//`. So, Zed will convert `%s:/\\(a\\)(b)/\\1/` into a search "
"for \"(a)(b)\" and a replacement of \"$1\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/vim.md:673
msgid ""
"For the full syntax supported by Zed's regex engine [see the regex crate "
"documentation](https://docs.rs/regex/latest/regex/#syntax)."
msgstr ""
